tr" style="line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:12pt;" role="presentation"><span style="font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;">Begin Your Study Journey in Japan</span></p></li></ol><p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.38;margin-top:12pt;margin-bottom:12pt;"><span style="font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;">Our experienced counsellors support you at every stage to ensure a smooth application experience.</span></p><p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.38;margin-top:12pt;margin-bottom:12pt;"><b style="font-weight:normal;"><br></b></p><h2 dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.38;margin-top:24pt;margin-bottom:6pt;"><span style="font-size:16pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;">Financial Requirements</span></h2><p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.38;margin-top:12pt;margin-bottom:12pt;"><span style="font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;">International students must demonstrate sufficient financial resources to cover tuition fees and living expenses in Japan. The required amount depends on your institution, course, study duration, and sponsor\'s financial background.</span></p><p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.38;margin-top:12pt;margin-bottom:12pt;"><span style="font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;">You\'ll generally need to provide documents such as bank statements, income certificates, sponsorship letters, and proof of the source of funds.</span></p><p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.38;margin-top:12pt;margin-bottom:12pt;"><span style="font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;">Our experts will guide you in preparing the appropriate financial documents according to your chosen institution\'s requirements.</span></p>',
            'faqs' => '[{"question":"Can I study in Japan after +2 in Nepal?","answer":"Yes \\u2014 if you meet the academic, language and financial requirements of your chosen school (language school, vocational college or bachelor\'s)."},{"question":"Do I need Japanese before applying?","answer":"Depends on the route. Language schools generally expect proof of basic study; Japanese-taught vocational and university programmes need a stronger level. Some university courses are English-taught, but Japanese still helps day to day."},{"question":"Is IELTS required?","answer":"Not always. English-taught programmes may ask for IELTS\\/TOEFL; Japanese-taught courses lean on JLPT, EJU or the school\'s own test."},{"question":"What Japanese level do I need?","answer":"It varies by school \\u2014 from beginner-with-proof-of-study for language schools, to a stronger level for vocational colleges and Japanese-taught universities. Always confirm with the specific institution."},{"question":"Can I work while studying?","answer":"Yes, after receiving official permission \\u2014 up to 28 hours\\/week during term, and up to 8 hours\\/day during long holidays."},{"question":"How much does it cost to live in Japan?","answer":"Around \\u00a5105,000\\/month on national average, though actual costs depend on your city, accommodation and lifestyle."},{"question":"Is a study gap accepted?","answer":"There\'s no universal rule \\u2014 gaps need an honest explanation and supporting documents. The final call rests with the school and immigration authorities."},{"question":"What is a COE?","answer":"Certificate of Eligibility \\u2014 a key document in the visa process, normally applied for by your accepting school once your application and financial documents are cleared."},{"question":"Do Nepali students need a TB Clearance Certificate?","answer":"Generally yes, for medium- to long-term stays, via Japan\'s Pre-Entry TB Screening (JPETS) at an approved clinic \\u2014 subject to current rules and exemptions."},{"question":"Are scholarships available?","answer":"Yes \\u2014 MEXT, JASSO, private and school-level options exist, but they\'re competitive and rarely cover full costs."},{"question":"When should I start my application?","answer":"6\\u201312 months before your target intake, to leave room for language prep, documentation, TB screening, COE and visa processing."},{"question":"Can Global Journey help with the whole process?","answer":"Yes \\u2014 language preparation, school selection, documentation, application, COE, visa preparation and pre-departure support, start to finish."}]',
            'quick_info_items' => '[{"icon":"bi bi-globe","title":"Country","value":"Japan"},{"icon":"bi bi-city","title":"Capital City","value":"Tokyo"},{"icon":"bi bi-speaking","title":"Language","value":"Japanese"},{"icon":"bi bi-students","title":"International Students","value":"over 300,000"},{"icon":"bi bi-weather","title":"Popular Intakes","value":"April & October"},{"icon":"bi bi-work","title":"Part-time Work","value":"Up to 28 hours per week (with permission)"},{"icon":"bi bi-globe","title":"Major Destination","value":"Tokyo, Kyoto, Chiba, Osaka, Kobe, Saitama, Sendai, Fukuoka, Hiroshima, Fukuyama, Nagoya, Gifu, Sapporo, Hokkaido, Nagano, Nakano, Okinawa, Khagosima, Nara"}]',
            'key_highlights' => '[{"text":"Globally recognized universities and colleges"},{"text":"Affordable tuition compared to many Western countries"},{"text":"Multiple study pathways including language schools and universities"},{"text":"Scholarship opportunities for international students"},{"text":"Safe and clean environment"},{"text":"Part-time work opportunities (subject to immigration permission)"},{"text":"Excellent public transportation"},{"text":"Strong employment opportunities after graduation"},{"text":"World leader in technology, engineering, robotics, and innovation"},{"text":"One of the most popular destinations for Nepali students"}]',
